440
00:17:24,644 --> 00:17:26,679
WHAT AM I GONNA DO
WITH MY LIFE NOW?"

441
00:17:26,679 --> 00:17:28,581
THAT'S THE TYPE OF DEDICATION
THAT I NEED FROM EACH

442
00:17:28,581 --> 00:17:30,917
AND EVERY SINGLE ONE OF YOU.

443
00:17:30,917 --> 00:17:32,018
EVERY WEEK ONE
OF YOU GUYS

444
00:17:32,018 --> 00:17:34,153
IS GONNA GO HOME.

445
00:17:34,153 --> 00:17:36,389
EVERY WEEK SOMEBODY'S GONNA BE
HEARTBROKEN, AND THERE'S ONLY

446
00:17:36,389 --> 00:17:39,492
GONNA BE ONE PERSON REMAINING.

447
00:17:39,492 --> 00:17:41,928
BUT I HAVE LOVE
FOR EVERY SINGLE ONE OF YOU,

448
00:17:41,928 --> 00:17:44,030
SO I WANNA PASS SOMETHING OUT
FOR EVERYBODY.

449
00:17:46,432 --> 00:17:48,601
I DESIGNED THESE MYSELF
JUST FOR Y'ALL.

450
00:17:48,601 --> 00:17:50,970
Women: OH, MY GOD!

451
00:17:50,970 --> 00:17:52,305
April: WHAT'S MOST BEAUTIFUL
ABOUT THIS GIFT

452
00:17:52,305 --> 00:17:53,806
IS WHAT IT REPRESENTS.

453
00:17:53,806 --> 00:17:56,409
WOW, TYRA BANKS SEES SOMETHING
IN ME THAT'S WORTH SOMETHING?

454
00:17:56,409 --> 00:17:58,711
MY GOD. THAT'S AMAZING.

455
00:17:58,711 --> 00:18:00,513
Shandi: FOR MY EYES TO GET
KINDA WATERY JUST KINDA

456
00:18:00,513 --> 00:18:04,050
SURPRISED ME
AND I'M THINKING, "WOW,

457
00:18:04,050 --> 00:18:05,818
I'M REALLY DOING THIS."

458
00:18:05,818 --> 00:18:07,053
Tyra: COME ON.

459
00:18:07,053 --> 00:18:08,788
LOVE, LOVE,
LOVE, LOVE, LOVE.

460
00:18:08,788 --> 00:18:12,525
Mercedes: TYRA IS MAKING ME
WANT THIS COMPETITION EVEN MORE.

461
00:18:12,525 --> 00:18:13,960
Women: AW!

462
00:18:13,960 --> 00:18:14,894
♪♪♪

463
00:18:16,228 --> 00:18:17,330
Xiomara: (haughty voice)
TONIGHT WE'RE HAVING DINNER

464
00:18:17,330 --> 00:18:19,932
AT THE TAVERN ON THE GREEN.

465
00:18:19,932 --> 00:18:22,134
Camille: TAVERN ON THE GREEN
IS A FABULOUS RESTAURANT,

466
00:18:22,134 --> 00:18:24,937
AND IT TAKES A VERY LONG TIME
TO GET A RESERVATION THERE.

467
00:18:24,937 --> 00:18:25,938
(dishes clatter)

468
00:18:25,938 --> 00:18:27,106
April: OH, SHOOT.

469
00:18:27,106 --> 00:18:28,374
Women: (laughing)

470
00:18:28,374 --> 00:18:29,542
April: I DON'T KNOW
WHAT YOU'RE SAYING.

471
00:18:29,542 --> 00:18:30,977
Bethany: WE HAVE
NO TOILET PAPER IN THERE?

472
00:18:30,977 --> 00:18:33,346
Sara: WE HAVE PAPER TOWELS.
Yoanna: BUT THEY DO HERE.

473
00:18:33,346 --> 00:18:36,015
I'LL BE RIGHT BACK.
Women: NO!

474
00:18:36,015 --> 00:18:38,117
Camille: YOU DON'T GO TO
A VERY EXPENSIVE,

475
00:18:38,117 --> 00:18:42,355
CLASSY RESTAURANT AND STEAL
TOILET PAPER.

476
00:18:42,355 --> 00:18:44,090
IT'S EMBARRASSING.

477
00:18:44,090 --> 00:18:46,158
Yoanna: PRESENT!

478
00:18:46,158 --> 00:18:47,660
Catie: I FEEL LIKE THOSE
OLD LADIES WHO, LIKE, TAKE

479
00:18:47,660 --> 00:18:49,328
THE SALT/PEPPER SHAKERS
AND STUFF.

480
00:18:49,328 --> 00:18:50,930
Camille: I WAS KINDA
DISAPPOINTED IN SEEING HOW

481
00:18:50,930 --> 00:18:52,365
THE GIRLS CONDUCTED THEMSELVES.

482
00:18:52,365 --> 00:18:55,167
DON'T PUT YOUR ELBOWS
ON THE TABLE, OR YOU DON'T

483
00:18:55,167 --> 00:18:57,737
TAKE UP AN ENTIRE PIECE OF BREAD
AND PUT, LIKE, FIVE THINGS

484
00:18:57,737 --> 00:19:00,139
OF BUTTER IN IT, AND, LIKE,
SHOVE THE WHOLE THING

485
00:19:00,139 --> 00:19:01,407
IN YOUR MOUTH.

486
00:19:01,407 --> 00:19:04,477
MAYBE I'M JUST A LITTLE BIT MORE
EDUCATED THAN SOME

487
00:19:04,477 --> 00:19:05,544
OF THE OTHER GIRLS.

488
00:19:05,544 --> 00:19:07,713
April: THANK YOU. TYRA MAIL.

489
00:19:07,713 --> 00:19:08,714
"HEY, LADIES.

490
00:19:08,714 --> 00:19:10,116
IT'S YOUR BIRTHDAY.

491
00:19:10,116 --> 00:19:12,752
YOU'RE GONNA WORK THE LENS
LIKE IT'S YOUR FIRST DAY..."

492
00:19:12,752 --> 00:19:15,655
Xiomara: YES!
April: "BE READY AT 6 A.M.

493
00:19:15,655 --> 00:19:17,923
FOR YOUR FIRST PHOTO SHOOT."

494
00:19:17,923 --> 00:19:19,492
Xiomara: THANK YOU,
THANK YOU.

495
00:19:19,492 --> 00:19:21,661
April: I HAVE NO CLUE
WHAT TO EXPECT.

496
00:19:21,661 --> 00:19:24,397
I DON'T KNOW IF I'M GONNA HAVE
TO BE WEARING A THONG

497
00:19:24,397 --> 00:19:27,366
OR AN EVENING GOWN OR WHAT.

498
00:19:27,366 --> 00:19:29,802
I WILL TOTALLY MAKE SURE
THAT I WAKE EVERY SINGLE ONE

499
00:19:29,802 --> 00:19:31,037
OF YOU UP.

500
00:19:31,037 --> 00:19:32,271
Jenascia: APRIL IS
THE DEFINITION OF "NICE."

501
00:19:32,271 --> 00:19:33,739
SHE'S THAT SWEET OF A PERSON.

502
00:19:33,739 --> 00:19:35,374
April: OKAY, GUYS,
I'LL SET MY ALARM,

503
00:19:35,374 --> 00:19:37,276
'CAUSE I HAVE MY OWN ALARM,
AND I'LL GO AROUND AND SQUEEZE

504
00:19:37,276 --> 00:19:39,612
ALL YOUR LITTLE TOES,
AND WE'LL ALL BE UP, OKAY?

505
00:19:39,612 --> 00:19:41,480
Sara: WE NEED SLEEP.
Catie: ALL RIGHT, LET'S GO.

506
00:19:42,915 --> 00:19:44,450
Camille: CAN I HAVE MY COAT,
PLEASE?

507
00:19:44,450 --> 00:19:45,818
♪♪♪

508
00:19:52,558 --> 00:19:53,793
(alarm clock buzzing)

509
00:19:55,594 --> 00:19:57,329
Heather: WE KNOW WE'RE GOING
ON A PHOTO SHOOT,

510
00:19:57,329 --> 00:19:58,898
AND THAT'S ALL WE KNEW.

511
00:19:58,898 --> 00:19:59,899
Bethany: WE ALL HAD
30 MINUTES TO GET DONE.

512
00:19:59,899 --> 00:20:00,900
WE ALL HAVE TO GET
IN THE SHOWER.

513
00:20:00,900 --> 00:20:02,268
WE ALL HAVE TO DO OUR HAIR.

514
00:20:02,268 --> 00:20:04,036
WE'RE ALL JUST GOING QUICK,
QUICK, QUICK, QUICK, QUICK.

515
00:20:04,036 --> 00:20:07,273
WE HAVE TO GET GOING,
AND NOBODY'S REALLY PAYING

516
00:20:07,273 --> 00:20:08,941
ATTENTION TO WHO'S HERE
AND WHO'S NOT.

517
00:20:08,941 --> 00:20:11,343
♪♪♪

518
00:20:14,947 --> 00:20:16,015
April: WHERE'S JENASCIA?

519
00:20:20,252 --> 00:20:21,887
April: IF I RUN UPSTAIRS,
ARE YOU GUYS GONNA MAKE SURE

520
00:20:21,887 --> 00:20:23,189
THEY DON'T LEAVE WITHOUT ME,
OR NO?

521
00:20:23,189 --> 00:20:24,657
PROBABLY NOT, RIGHT?

522
00:20:24,657 --> 00:20:27,159
Anna: RUN UP INSIDE AND SEE.

523
00:20:27,159 --> 00:20:29,528
April: WHEN I REALIZED
THAT JENASCIA IS NOT WITH US,

524
00:20:29,528 --> 00:20:33,032
I AM NOT ABLE TO HELP HER OUT
AND GET HER IN THAT VAN

525
00:20:33,032 --> 00:20:35,201
WITHOUT JEOPARDIZING
EVERY SINGLE OTHER PERSON'S

526
00:20:35,201 --> 00:20:37,036
ABILITY TO GET TO THE SHOOT.

527
00:20:37,036 --> 00:20:40,005
SHE HELPED ME OUT ON THE RUNWAY,
AND THAT'S TEARING ME UP INSIDE.

528
00:20:40,005 --> 00:20:41,674
Mercedes: BASICALLY,
IT'S SURVIVAL OF THE FITTEST.

529
00:20:41,674 --> 00:20:44,643
JENASCIA DIDN'T WAKE UP.
THAT'S HER OWN DAMN FAULT,

530
00:20:44,643 --> 00:20:47,146
AND WE CAN'T BABYSIT
EVERYBODY ELSE.

531
00:20:55,354 --> 00:20:57,056
Yoanna: WE'RE ON OUR WAY
TO THE FIRST PHOTO SHOOT EVER,

532
00:20:57,056 --> 00:20:58,457
AND WE DON'T KNOW
WHAT TO EXPECT,

533
00:20:58,457 --> 00:21:01,060
AND JENASCIA DIDN'T MAKE IT
BECAUSE SHE DIDN'T WAKE UP.

534
00:21:03,262 --> 00:21:04,263
Nigel: COME IN. COME IN.

535
00:21:04,263 --> 00:21:05,798
WELCOME TO
INDUSTRIA STUDIOS.

536
00:21:05,798 --> 00:21:07,500
I'M NIGEL BARKER.

537
00:21:07,500 --> 00:21:10,102
I'M GONNA BE YOUR PHOTOGRAPHER
FOR YOUR FIRST FASHION SHOOT

538
00:21:10,102 --> 00:21:11,537
FOR "AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL."

539
00:21:11,537 --> 00:21:14,707
TODAY WE'RE GONNA DO AN AD FOR
FRESHLOOK COLOR CONTACT LENSES.

540
00:21:14,707 --> 00:21:18,210
THE THEME FOR TODAY'S SHOOT
IS THE GARDEN OF EDEN.

541
00:21:18,210 --> 00:21:19,345
IT'S GONNA BE REALLY BEAUTIFUL.

542
00:21:19,345 --> 00:21:21,514
EACH ONE OF YOU HAS HAD
A COMPLETE OUTFIT

543
00:21:21,514 --> 00:21:23,315
DESIGNED FOR YOU BY BODY CAST.

544
00:21:23,315 --> 00:21:24,617
Ed: WHAT WE'RE GONNA DO
TODAY IS WE'RE GONNA

545
00:21:24,617 --> 00:21:26,719
TRANSFORM YOU INTO A VISION
OF ORIGINAL BEAUTY--

546
00:21:26,719 --> 00:21:28,354
EVE IN THE GARDEN OF EDEN.

547
00:21:28,354 --> 00:21:31,190
AND THIS IS THE MAJOR PART
OF YOUR COSTUME RIGHT HERE.

548
00:21:31,190 --> 00:21:34,326
YOUR BODY'S GONNA BE COVERED
IN JEWELS AND BODY PAINT.

549
00:21:34,326 --> 00:21:35,861
DOES ANYBODY HAVE
ANY QUESTIONS ABOUT THE PROCESS

550
00:21:35,861 --> 00:21:37,696
OR WHAT'S GONNA HAPPEN TODAY?

551
00:21:37,696 --> 00:21:39,932
Anna: SO OUR WHOLE BODY'S
GONNA BE COVERED IN THE PAINT?

552
00:21:39,932 --> 00:21:41,133
Nigel: YEAH.

553
00:21:41,133 --> 00:21:42,701
Ed: YOUR BODIES WILL BE
COVERED IN PAINT, YES.

554
00:21:42,701 --> 00:21:45,004
Nigel: BUT OBVIOUSLY,
YOU ARE GONNA BE NUDE,

555
00:21:45,004 --> 00:21:46,939
BUT YOU ARE GONNA BE COVERED
FROM HEAD TO TOE.

556
00:21:46,939 --> 00:21:49,542
IT'S INCREDIBLY INTRICATE.

557
00:21:49,542 --> 00:21:50,576
Xiomara: NUDITY'S GREAT.

558
00:21:50,576 --> 00:21:52,778
I'M ALL ABOUT IT. BRING IT ON.

559
00:21:52,778 --> 00:21:54,113
Anna: I DIDN'T APPRECIATE
THAT.

560
00:21:54,113 --> 00:21:57,383
YOU KNOW, IT'S JUST NOT BEING
LADYLIKE, AND YOU KNOW,

561
00:21:57,383 --> 00:22:00,186
I DO FEEL THAT I REPRESENT
THE MOMS AND THE WIVES

562
00:22:00,186 --> 00:22:02,454
OF THE U.S.,
I GUESS LIKE A ROLE MODEL,

563
00:22:02,454 --> 00:22:05,124
AND I DO ACCEPT
THAT RESPONSIBILITY.

564
00:22:05,124 --> 00:22:07,326
Nigel: I SEE WE ONLY HAVE 11.

565
00:22:07,326 --> 00:22:08,761
WHAT'S THAT ABOUT?

566
00:22:08,761 --> 00:22:11,230
April: JENASCIA'S NOT THERE,
AND I NOTICED THAT HER COSTUME

567
00:22:11,230 --> 00:22:13,365
IS PROBABLY THE MOST ELABORATE
ONE OF ALL OF THEM,

568
00:22:13,365 --> 00:22:15,568
AND THAT REALLY HITS ME HARD,
BECAUSE IT MAKES IT

569
00:22:15,568 --> 00:22:17,770
EVEN MORE APPARENT
THAT SHE'S NOT THERE.

570
00:22:17,770 --> 00:22:19,505
Nigel: WE'LL HAVE TO GET
A WAKE-UP CALL IN TO HER.

571
00:22:19,505 --> 00:22:21,807
Heather: JENASCIA
NOT MAKING IT TO THE PHOTO SHOOT

572
00:22:21,807 --> 00:22:24,443
FOR THE--YOU KNOW,
THIS IS WHAT WE'RE HERE FOR.

573
00:22:24,443 --> 00:22:27,046
IF YOU'RE NOT REALLY THERE FOR
THE MODELING AND FOR THE SHOOT,

574
00:22:27,046 --> 00:22:30,616
THEN YOU'RE GONNA BE... OUT.

575
00:22:30,616 --> 00:22:33,919
(telephone rings)

576
00:22:33,919 --> 00:22:37,056
(ring)

577
00:22:37,056 --> 00:22:38,424
(ring)

578
00:22:41,260 --> 00:22:42,661
Sara: I DIDN'T SHAKE HER.
Jim: DID ANYONE TOUCH HER?

579
00:22:42,661 --> 00:22:43,963
Sara: NO. I DON'T KNOW.

580
00:22:43,963 --> 00:22:45,731
I WAS, LIKE, THE SECOND ONE
IN THE HOUSE TO WAKE UP.

581
00:22:45,731 --> 00:22:46,966
Jim: WELL, YOU GUYS
ARE HER ROOMMATES.

582
00:22:46,966 --> 00:22:48,534
Sara: SO?

583
00:22:48,534 --> 00:22:50,569
JENASCIA, I LOVE YOU,
BUT I FEEL LIKE SHE NEEDS TO

584
00:22:50,569 --> 00:22:51,837
TAKE ACCOUNTABILITY FOR THAT.

585
00:22:51,837 --> 00:22:53,973
I DON'T FEEL LIKE
I HAVE TO JUSTIFY MYSELF.

586
00:22:53,973 --> 00:22:56,842
Bethany: I DIDN'T KNOW
I HAD TO PLAY MOM TODAY.

587
00:22:56,842 --> 00:22:58,410
SOMEBODY SHOULD HAVE TOLD ME.

588
00:22:58,410 --> 00:22:59,612
Jim: WHEN YOU GUYS TRIED
TO WAKE UP JENASCIA,

589
00:22:59,612 --> 00:23:00,946
WHAT HAPPENED?

590
00:23:00,946 --> 00:23:03,449
Shandi: SHE DIDN'T WAKE UP.
Jim: SHE WAS BREATHING?

591
00:23:03,449 --> 00:23:05,251
Shandi: YEAH.

592
00:23:05,251 --> 00:23:08,654
(telephone rings)

593
00:23:08,654 --> 00:23:10,956
(ring)

594
00:23:13,125 --> 00:23:14,326
Jenascia: Hello?

595
00:23:14,326 --> 00:23:15,728
Jim: IS THIS JENASCIA?
Jenascia: I DON'T KNOW

596
00:23:15,728 --> 00:23:17,763
WHAT THE HELL JUST HAPPENED.

597
00:23:17,763 --> 00:23:19,632
I THOUGHT I WOULD HEAR
THEIR ALARM CLOCK,

598
00:23:19,632 --> 00:23:21,500
OR AT LEAST THEM.

599
00:23:21,500 --> 00:23:23,535
OR MAYBE SOMEONE WOULD
WAKE ME UP, BUT I DON'T KNOW

600
00:23:23,535 --> 00:23:25,304
HOW THIS HAPPENED.

601
00:23:25,304 --> 00:23:27,072
Jim: JUST GET YOURSELF
TOGETHER AND GET HERE A.S.A.P.

602
00:23:28,874 --> 00:23:30,509
Jenascia: (bleep) BITCHES.

603
00:23:30,509 --> 00:23:32,177
♪♪♪

604
00:23:39,618 --> 00:23:40,619
Bethany: YEAH,
I'VE NEVER BEEN BLUE.

605
00:23:40,619 --> 00:23:41,620
I FEEL LIKE A SMURF.

606
00:23:41,620 --> 00:23:43,989
Sara: CHAINS ON NAKED BODY.

607
00:23:43,989 --> 00:23:45,524
I HAVEN'T DONE THAT BEFORE.

608
00:23:45,524 --> 00:23:46,992
♪♪♪

609
00:24:01,140 --> 00:24:02,408
Jenascia: I KNOW
IT'S NEW YORK TRAFFIC,

610
00:24:02,408 --> 00:24:05,444
BUT I'LL PAY YOU DOUBLE
IF YOU CAN GET THERE FAST.

611
00:24:05,444 --> 00:24:06,812
Nigel: OKAY, LADIES.

612
00:24:06,812 --> 00:24:08,113
NOW IT'S SHOW TIME.

613
00:24:08,113 --> 00:24:10,282
EVERY EVE MUST
HAVE AN ADAM.

614
00:24:10,282 --> 00:24:12,651
LET ME BRING IN THE ADAMS.

615
00:24:14,853 --> 00:24:17,823
Heather: THE MALE MODELS--
THE ADAMS--THEY ARE

616
00:24:17,823 --> 00:24:20,426
REALLY, REALLY GOOD-LOOKING.

617
00:24:20,426 --> 00:24:22,695
Nigel: ALL RIGHT, GUYS.

618
00:24:22,695 --> 00:24:25,331
Sara: ADAM WAS RIGHT THERE,
YOU KNOW, WITH EVERYTHING

619
00:24:25,331 --> 00:24:26,398
HANGING OUT.

620
00:24:26,398 --> 00:24:27,833
(chuckles)

621
00:24:28,934 --> 00:24:31,070
Nigel: SARA--
SHE WAS A LITTLE SCARED.

622
00:24:31,070 --> 00:24:32,571
BUT I MEAN, I'D LIKE TO
SEE MORE FROM HER.

623
00:24:32,571 --> 00:24:33,939
MOVE YOUR BODY AROUND
SO I SEE THAT SIDE

624
00:24:33,939 --> 00:24:35,074
OF YOUR BODY REALLY NICE.

625
00:24:35,074 --> 00:24:36,608
THERE YOU GO.

626
00:24:36,608 --> 00:24:37,843
BETHANY NEEDS TO WORK
ON HER MOVEMENT.

627
00:24:37,843 --> 00:24:38,978
BUT YOU KNOW WHAT?

628
00:24:38,978 --> 00:24:40,746
WHEN WE HAVE AN INCREDIBLE
GARDEN OF EDEN,

629
00:24:40,746 --> 00:24:44,016
AND WE NEEDED SOMEONE WITH
SOME EXHIBITIONIST QUALITIES.

630
00:24:44,016 --> 00:24:45,784
SHE CERTAINLY HAD THEM.

631
00:24:45,784 --> 00:24:46,986
THAT'S NICE.

632
00:24:46,986 --> 00:24:48,120
♪♪♪

633
00:24:52,057 --> 00:24:53,826
Jenascia: HELLO?

634
00:24:53,826 --> 00:24:56,929
Nigel: APRIL, OUR ASIAN EVE,
WAS GORGEOUS.

635
00:24:56,929 --> 00:24:58,230
HER BODY IS FANTASTIC.

636
00:24:58,230 --> 00:24:59,431
HER FACE IS FANTASTIC.

637
00:24:59,431 --> 00:25:00,699
MY GOODNESS ME.

638
00:25:00,699 --> 00:25:02,267
THAT'S EXACTLY WHAT
I'M LOOKING FOR.

639
00:25:09,508 --> 00:25:10,542
Nigel: NIGEL.

640
00:25:10,542 --> 00:25:11,944
Jenascia: NICE TO MEET YOU.

641
00:25:11,944 --> 00:25:14,013
Nigel: YOU'RE A LITTLE LATE.

642
00:25:14,013 --> 00:25:15,614
IT'S OKAY. IT'S ALL RIGHT.

643
00:25:15,614 --> 00:25:17,883
IT'S OKAY. YEAH. COME HERE.

644
00:25:17,883 --> 00:25:19,018
COME HERE.

645
00:25:19,018 --> 00:25:20,019
Jenascia: OH, MY GOD.

646
00:25:20,019 --> 00:25:21,620
THIS IS NOT REALLY HAPPENING.

647
00:25:21,620 --> 00:25:24,390
I WAS SO NAIVE TO THINK
THAT THE OTHER GIRLS WERE

648
00:25:24,390 --> 00:25:27,192
ACTUALLY GONNA HELP ME OUT,
EVEN THOUGH I HAD HELPED

649
00:25:27,192 --> 00:25:29,561
SOME OF THEM OUT.

650
00:25:29,561 --> 00:25:32,064
YOU KNOW, LIKE WITH APRIL--
I HELPED HER.

651
00:25:32,064 --> 00:25:36,235
I... HELPED HER SO MUCH
ON THAT FIRST FASHION SHOW.

652
00:25:36,235 --> 00:25:38,537
SHE SHOULD BE KISSING
THE... GROUND THAT I WALK ON

653
00:25:38,537 --> 00:25:39,538
RIGHT NOW.

654
00:25:39,538 --> 00:25:40,539
I'LL BE FINE.

655
00:25:40,539 --> 00:25:41,707
Nigel: IT'S OKAY, THOUGH.

656
00:25:41,707 --> 00:25:42,808
IT REALLY--
WE'RE GONNA DEAL WITH IT.

657
00:25:42,808 --> 00:25:44,009
Jenascia: I'M MORE MAD
THAN ANYTHING.

658
00:25:44,009 --> 00:25:45,878
Nigel: I KNOW,
BUT YOU NEED TO LET THAT GO.

659
00:25:45,878 --> 00:25:47,379
BOTTOM LINE IS YOU MADE IT.

660
00:25:47,379 --> 00:25:50,916
RIGHT NOW WHAT WOULD BE MORE
OF A PROBLEM FOR ME IS NOT

661
00:25:50,916 --> 00:25:52,484
THE FACT THAT YOU'RE LATE.

662
00:25:52,484 --> 00:25:53,619
THE BIG PROBLEM RIGHT NOW
IS THAT YOU'RE UPSET.

663
00:25:53,619 --> 00:25:55,054
Jenascia: THE WATERWORKS.

664
00:25:55,054 --> 00:25:56,722
Nigel: YOU WANT TO SORT OF
SAY, "DAMN IT, YOU WERE LATE,

665
00:25:56,722 --> 00:25:57,990
YOU KNOW? WHAT IS THIS?"

666
00:25:57,990 --> 00:25:58,991
BUT I CAN'T.

667
00:25:58,991 --> 00:26:00,492
WE HAVE TO KEEP ALL THAT IN.

668
00:26:00,492 --> 00:26:01,994
I HAVE TO CAPTURE A SHOT.

669
00:26:01,994 --> 00:26:04,096
Jenascia: BITCHES!

670
00:26:04,096 --> 00:26:05,464
Nigel: WE HAVE A LONG DAY
AHEAD OF US,

671
00:26:05,464 --> 00:26:07,399
AND WE HAVE OTHER THINGS TO DO
OTHER THAN TAKE CARE

672
00:26:07,399 --> 00:26:08,567
OF ONE GIRL.

673
00:26:08,567 --> 00:26:09,902
♪♪♪

674
00:26:11,937 --> 00:26:12,971
Nigel: TWIST YOUR LEG AROUND
A BIT.

675
00:26:12,971 --> 00:26:14,139
SWING THE OTHER WAY.

676
00:26:16,275 --> 00:26:17,276
Nigel: BEAUTIFUL.

677
00:26:17,276 --> 00:26:18,844
Catie: I GOT
THE HEAVENLY EVE,

678
00:26:18,844 --> 00:26:22,147
WHICH WAS BASICALLY A PAINTING
OF, LIKE, THE SISTINE CHAPEL--

679
00:26:22,147 --> 00:26:23,649
THE CEILING OF IT--ON ME.

680
00:26:23,649 --> 00:26:25,117
Nigel: CATIE--
I THOUGHT FOR A MOMENT

681
00:26:25,117 --> 00:26:29,121
SHE WAS GONNA BE A FAINTER,
SHE WAS LIKE... ON THE CAMERA.

682
00:26:29,121 --> 00:26:31,123
CHIN UP. EYES UP HIGH.

683
00:26:31,123 --> 00:26:32,424
Anna: I SAT THERE
IN THE ROOM AND I SAW

684
00:26:32,424 --> 00:26:34,460
THESE GIRLS--
THEIR COOCHIE WAS SHOWIN',

685
00:26:34,460 --> 00:26:37,096
THEIR BREASTS WERE HANGIN' OUT,
AND NIPPLES SHOWIN',

686
00:26:37,096 --> 00:26:39,932
AND PLUS THE MALE MODEL
IS DOWN THERE, YOU KNOW,

687
00:26:39,932 --> 00:26:42,468
WHERE YOUR PRIVATE PARTY IS.

688
00:26:42,468 --> 00:26:43,735
Man: IT'S JUST A DOT
RIGHT HERE.

689
00:26:43,735 --> 00:26:45,170
Anna: I DON'T WANNA BE
A PART OF THAT.

690
00:26:45,170 --> 00:26:48,841
I CAN'T JUST IMAGINE
SOMEONE ELSE HERE AND DOWN THERE

691
00:26:48,841 --> 00:26:50,642
EXCEPT MY HUSBAND, YOU KNOW?

692
00:26:50,642 --> 00:26:52,911
AND IF I SHOW IT
TO THE WHOLE WORLD, YOU KNOW,

693
00:26:52,911 --> 00:26:54,546
WHAT'S SO SPECIAL WHEN I...

694
00:26:54,546 --> 00:26:55,714
(crying)

695
00:26:57,449 --> 00:26:59,251
I JUST CAN'T--I CAN'T DO IT.

696
00:26:59,251 --> 00:27:00,619
I'M VERY UNCOMFORTABLE.

697
00:27:00,619 --> 00:27:02,521
I CANNOT DO IT, YOU KNOW?

698
00:27:02,521 --> 00:27:04,223
I HAVE TO...

699
00:27:04,223 --> 00:27:05,791
YOU KNOW,
THIS IS FOR MY HUSBAND.

700
00:27:05,791 --> 00:27:08,360
I CAN'T SHOW NO ONE ELSE.

701
00:27:08,360 --> 00:27:09,428
Yohanca: RIGHT.

702
00:27:09,428 --> 00:27:11,330
Anna: I'M NOT GONNA DO IT.

703
00:27:11,330 --> 00:27:13,799
Catie: ANNA--YOU KNOW,
SHE'S IN A DIFFERENT PLACE

704
00:27:13,799 --> 00:27:14,933
IN HER LIFE.

705
00:27:14,933 --> 00:27:16,535
SHE HAS A SON
AND SHE HAS A HUSBAND.

706
00:27:16,535 --> 00:27:18,604
DO YOU RETOUCH SO NONE OF
THE NIPPLES SHOW AND THAT STUFF?

707
00:27:18,604 --> 00:27:20,706
Nigel: THINGS LIKE THAT,
YEAH.

708
00:27:20,706 --> 00:27:21,807
THEY'RE NOT GONNA BE SHOWING.

709
00:27:21,807 --> 00:27:22,841
WE CAN'T DO THAT.

710
00:27:22,841 --> 00:27:24,076
AND THIS
IS AN IMPORTANT THING.

711
00:27:24,076 --> 00:27:26,145
IT'D BE A REAL SHAME
FOR YOU NOT TO BE

712
00:27:26,145 --> 00:27:27,813
PARTICIPATING IN IT,
AND WE'LL MARCH YOU UP

713
00:27:27,813 --> 00:27:30,282
TO THE SET,
HIDE YOU WITH A GOWN,

714
00:27:30,282 --> 00:27:32,217
DO WHATEVER WE NEED TO DO.

715
00:27:32,217 --> 00:27:33,619
Anna: AND IT'S GONNA BE
THE SAME ANSWER, SO...

716
00:27:33,619 --> 00:27:35,087
Nigel: OKAY.

717
00:27:35,087 --> 00:27:36,488
WELL, THAT BEING SAID, THEN,
I'M SORRY, BUT I'M GONNA HAVE

718
00:27:36,488 --> 00:27:38,023
TO ASK YOU TO LEAVE.

719
00:27:38,023 --> 00:27:39,992
I'M SORRY.

720
00:27:39,992 --> 00:27:41,793
Anna: AND HE THOUGHT THAT
IF I DIDN'T WANNA BE A PART

721
00:27:41,793 --> 00:27:45,330
OF IT, THEN YOU KNOW,
I SHOULDN'T BE IN HIS PRESENCE

722
00:27:45,330 --> 00:27:46,932
WHATSOEVER.

723
00:27:46,932 --> 00:27:48,133
Nigel: YOU KNOW WHAT?

724
00:27:48,133 --> 00:27:49,501
AT THIS POINT,
I JUST NEEDED A GIRL,

725
00:27:49,501 --> 00:27:51,570
BECAUSE WE HAVEN'T GOT TIME,
AND IT'S A REAL SHAME

726
00:27:51,570 --> 00:27:54,239
SHE WASN'T COMFORTABLE BEING
NUDE UNDER HER MAKEUP.

727
00:27:55,707 --> 00:27:57,643
Heather: I DON'T MIND
A REALLY HOT PHOTOGRAPHER

728
00:27:57,643 --> 00:27:58,977
LOOKING AT MY NAKED BODY.

729
00:27:58,977 --> 00:28:00,312
Nigel: HEATHER,
FIX YOUR EYES.

730
00:28:00,312 --> 00:28:02,948
BUT ACTUALLY FOR ME,
HER LOOK IS VERY CALIFORNIA.

731
00:28:02,948 --> 00:28:04,183
EYES UP HIGHER.

732
00:28:04,183 --> 00:28:06,118
MERCEDES--WHEN I WOULD
GIVE HER DIRECTION,

733
00:28:06,118 --> 00:28:08,253
SHE WOULD REMEMBER FOR MAYBE
ONLY ONE OR TWO FRAMES,

734
00:28:08,253 --> 00:28:10,455
AND SHE WOULD SLIP BACK
INTO WHAT SHE WAS DOING BEFORE.

735
00:28:10,455 --> 00:28:12,224
EYES UP OVER HERE. THERE.

736
00:28:12,224 --> 00:28:14,726
SHANDI NEEDS TO REALIZE
THAT SHE'S A BEAUTIFUL GIRL.

737
00:28:14,726 --> 00:28:16,762
FOR MODELING, YOU REALLY NEED
TO BE AWARE OF YOURSELF.

738
00:28:16,762 --> 00:28:17,763
THAT'S SOMETHING
THAT WILL COME IN TIME.

739
00:28:20,532 --> 00:28:23,769
YOANNA--HER FACE IS FANTASTIC,
BUT, YOU KNOW, HER BODY--

740
00:28:23,769 --> 00:28:26,205
COULD DO A LITTLE BIT OF WORK.

741
00:28:26,205 --> 00:28:27,472
Man: MALE AND FEMALE.

742
00:28:30,242 --> 00:28:32,644
Jenascia: I WAS A LITTLE BIT
TEARY, LIKE, ALL DAY,

743
00:28:32,644 --> 00:28:35,214
AND ALL I COULD THINK WAS,
"THOSE BITCHES."

744
00:28:35,214 --> 00:28:37,416
Nigel: CHIN UP FOR ME,
SWEETIE.

745
00:28:37,416 --> 00:28:39,651
THERE YOU GO.

746
00:28:39,651 --> 00:28:41,019
HOLD THE ARROW OF THE BOW DOWN.

747
00:28:41,019 --> 00:28:42,754
TWIST IT UP A LITTLE BIT.

748
00:28:42,754 --> 00:28:44,723
THE TOP PART OF THE BOW'S
A LITTLE HIGHER.

749
00:28:44,723 --> 00:28:46,558
PUT YOUR HAND ON YOUR HIP
FOR ME.

750
00:28:46,558 --> 00:28:47,559
YOU'VE GOT A BEAUTIFUL BODY.

751
00:28:47,559 --> 00:28:48,560
PLAY WITH IT.

752
00:28:48,560 --> 00:28:49,828
REAL ATTITUDY. BOOM.

753
00:28:49,828 --> 00:28:51,263
Xiomara: JENASCIA'S
NOT REALLY GETTING IT.

754
00:28:51,263 --> 00:28:54,299
NIGEL KEEPS ON TELLING HER,
"NO, DO THIS. LOOK THAT WAY.

755
00:28:54,299 --> 00:28:55,667
LOOK THAT WAY."

756
00:28:55,667 --> 00:28:57,769
YOU DON'T WANT A PHOTOGRAPHER
TO HAVE TO DIRECT YOU,

757
00:28:57,769 --> 00:28:59,371
BECAUSE THAT'S WHY
YOU'RE A MODEL.

758
00:28:59,371 --> 00:29:00,806
Nigel: NO, IT'S NOT--
NOT SO MUCH.

759
00:29:00,806 --> 00:29:02,574
JENASCIA BLEW IT
BEING LATE THIS MORNING.

760
00:29:02,574 --> 00:29:05,077
SHE REALLY DIDN'T
FULLY GET INTO IT,

761
00:29:05,077 --> 00:29:06,478
WHICH IS A SHAME.

762
00:29:06,478 --> 00:29:08,680
Jenascia: I DON'T KNOW WHY
THEY DIDN'T WAKE ME UP,

763
00:29:08,680 --> 00:29:12,451
BUT IF THIS DOESN'T
GET ME ELIMINATED, IT'S ON.

764
00:29:12,451 --> 00:29:14,219
IT'S SO (bleep) ON.

765
00:29:14,219 --> 00:29:15,654
I'M NOT PLAYING ANYMORE.

766
00:29:15,654 --> 00:29:19,992
I'M NOT GONNA BE NICE
AND HELP ANYONE ANYMORE.

767
00:29:19,992 --> 00:29:21,159
YOU DON'T HAVE
THE RIGHT CLOTHES ON,

768
00:29:21,159 --> 00:29:22,461
(bleep) YOU.

769
00:29:22,461 --> 00:29:23,629
THIS IS ABOUT ME NOW.

770
00:29:30,135 --> 00:29:32,638
Anna: I SAID NO
TO THE FACT OF POSING NUDE,

771
00:29:32,638 --> 00:29:35,841
AND NIGEL--HE ASKED ME
TO LEAVE THE SET AREA.

772
00:29:35,841 --> 00:29:38,610
I FELT LIKE IT DID NOT
JEOPARDIZED MY CHANCES AT ALL.

773
00:29:40,912 --> 00:29:42,214
Woman: (gasps)

774
00:29:42,214 --> 00:29:45,250
Women: (speaking
over each other)

775
00:29:45,250 --> 00:29:47,219
Anna: TYRA MAIL.

776
00:29:47,219 --> 00:29:50,489
"TOMORROW IS YOUR FIRST MEETING
WITH THE JUDGES.

777
00:29:50,489 --> 00:29:54,526
ONLY 11 OF YOU WILL CONTINUE ON
WITH THE HOPE OF BECOMING

778
00:29:54,526 --> 00:30:00,032
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL.
ONE OF YOU WILL BE ELIMINATED."

779
00:30:00,032 --> 00:30:02,501
♪♪♪

780
00:30:04,569 --> 00:30:06,238
Heather: REALITY HAS HIT ME.

781
00:30:06,238 --> 00:30:07,339
THERE'S AN ELIMINATION.

782
00:30:07,339 --> 00:30:08,507
THIS IS IT.

783
00:30:08,507 --> 00:30:10,108
THIS IS THE BOTTOM LINE.

784
00:30:10,108 --> 00:30:11,476
Shandi: IT'S A WEIRD DAY.

785
00:30:11,476 --> 00:30:12,978
JENASCIA THINKS
SHE'S GOING HOME

786
00:30:12,978 --> 00:30:14,613
BECAUSE SHE DIDN'T WAKE UP
ON TIME,

787
00:30:14,613 --> 00:30:16,181
AND, YOU KNOW, SHE WAS LATE.

788
00:30:16,181 --> 00:30:18,283
Jenascia: MAYBE I WAS
JUST SUPPOSED TO GO THIS FAR.

789
00:30:18,283 --> 00:30:19,751
♪♪♪

790
00:30:25,857 --> 00:30:28,293
Tyra: WOW, MY 12 FINALISTS.

791
00:30:28,293 --> 00:30:31,196
YOU GUYS ARE HERE
IN THE INFAMOUS JUDGING ROOM.

792
00:30:31,196 --> 00:30:33,231
WE HAVE OUR PANEL OF JUDGES.

793
00:30:33,231 --> 00:30:34,599
WE HAVE JANICE DICKINSON.

794
00:30:34,599 --> 00:30:37,035
JANICE WAS ONE
OF THE FIRST SUPERMODELS.

795
00:30:37,035 --> 00:30:40,339
Janice: MY JOB IS TO BE
AS BRUTALLY HONEST AS POSSIBLE,

796
00:30:40,339 --> 00:30:42,107
AND, HEY, LET'S FACE IT.

797
00:30:42,107 --> 00:30:44,810
IF THE GIRLS CAN'T HANDLE
MY CRITIQUE,

798
00:30:44,810 --> 00:30:46,845
THEY SURE ARE NOT GOING
TO BE ABLE TO HANDLE

799
00:30:46,845 --> 00:30:48,013
THE FASHION INDUSTRY.

800
00:30:48,013 --> 00:30:49,348
Tyra: NEXT,
WE HAVE ERIC NICHOLSON.

801
00:30:49,348 --> 00:30:53,952
ERIC IS THE SENIOR FASHION
EDITOR AT "JANE" MAGAZINE.

802
00:30:53,952 --> 00:30:56,355
Eric: WHAT I THINK
MAKES A TOP MODEL

803
00:30:56,355 --> 00:30:58,457
IS SOMEONE WHO ADDS
THAT EXTRA SOMETHING

804
00:30:58,457 --> 00:31:00,625
THAT A PHOTOGRAPHER
WANTS TO CAPTURE.

805
00:31:00,625 --> 00:31:03,495
Tyra: AND LAST BUT NOT LEAST,
I KNOW YOU GUYS DIDN'T KNOW,

806
00:31:03,495 --> 00:31:07,299
NIGEL BARKER IS
OUR PERMANENT JUDGE,

807
00:31:07,299 --> 00:31:08,333
NOT JUST JUDGE FOR TODAY.

808
00:31:08,333 --> 00:31:09,634
Nigel: HI, LADIES.

809
00:31:09,634 --> 00:31:11,803
WHAT I'M ALWAYS LOOKING FOR
IN A MODEL IS A MUSE,

810
00:31:11,803 --> 00:31:13,605
A FACE THAT'S GONNA INSPIRE ME.

811
00:31:13,605 --> 00:31:15,040
Tyra: NOW HERE'S THE PRIZES.

812
00:31:15,040 --> 00:31:17,209
YOU GET A CONTRACT
WITH IMG MODELS,

813
00:31:17,209 --> 00:31:18,910
ONE OF THE TOP
MANAGEMENT COMPANIES

814
00:31:18,910 --> 00:31:20,779
IN THE WORLD,
AND I HAVE BEEN WITH THEM

815
00:31:20,779 --> 00:31:22,581
FOR A NUMBER OF YEARS.

816
00:31:22,581 --> 00:31:25,117
YOU GET A COSMETICS CAMPAIGN
WITH SEPHORA,

817
00:31:25,117 --> 00:31:26,818
THE LEADING BEAUTY RETAILER.

818
00:31:26,818 --> 00:31:29,554
YOU WILL ALSO HAVE A SPREAD
IN "JANE" MAGAZINE,

819
00:31:29,554 --> 00:31:33,024
WHICH IS THE HIPPEST, TRENDIEST
MAGAZINE OUT THERE RIGHT NOW.

820
00:31:33,024 --> 00:31:34,192
NOW THERE'S A COUPLE OF THINGS
THAT YOU GUYS ARE GONNA

821
00:31:34,192 --> 00:31:35,527
BE JUDGED ON.

822
00:31:35,527 --> 00:31:37,562
FIRST, YOU'RE GONNA BE JUDGED ON
WHAT YOU JUST STRAIGHT

823
00:31:37,562 --> 00:31:38,597
WALKED IN HERE WITH.

824
00:31:38,597 --> 00:31:40,031
THAT'S YOUR NATURAL TALENT.

825
00:31:40,031 --> 00:31:42,300
THEN YOU'RE GONNA BE JUDGED
ON YOUR POTENTIAL.

826
00:31:42,300 --> 00:31:44,836
ALSO, YOUR PERSONALITY.

827
00:31:44,836 --> 00:31:46,938
THE FOURTH THING IS
YOUR ABILITY TO BE VERSATILE

828
00:31:46,938 --> 00:31:48,507
IN THE FASHION INDUSTRY.

829
00:31:48,507 --> 00:31:50,809
I'M LOOKING FOR SOMEBODY
THAT'S EDGY AND EDITORIAL

830
00:31:50,809 --> 00:31:52,644
IN HIGH FASHION,
AND I'M LOOKING FOR SOMEONE

831
00:31:52,644 --> 00:31:54,679
THAT CAN SMILE
AND SELL TOOTHPASTE.

832
00:31:54,679 --> 00:31:56,114
AND THE LAST THING
IS YOUR PERFORMANCE

833
00:31:56,114 --> 00:31:57,649
IN YOUR PHOTO SHOOTS.

834
00:31:57,649 --> 00:31:59,818
WE'RE GONNA BRING YOU IN
FOR YOUR INDIVIDUAL EVALUATIONS

835
00:31:59,818 --> 00:32:01,753
ONE BY ONE.

836
00:32:01,753 --> 00:32:06,358
WE'VE RANDOMLY DRAWN NAMES,
AND, XIOMARA, YOU'RE FIRST.

837
00:32:06,358 --> 00:32:07,959
SO HOW DID YOU FEEL
WHEN I TOLD YOU

838
00:32:07,959 --> 00:32:09,528
THAT YOU HAD TO DO
A SURPRISE FASHION SHOW?

839
00:32:09,528 --> 00:32:11,463
Xiomara: I WAS SHOCKED,
COMPLETELY SHOCKED.

840
00:32:11,463 --> 00:32:12,431
Tyra: HERE IT IS.

841
00:32:15,700 --> 00:32:17,102
Nigel: YOUR EYES
WEREN'T CONNECTING.

842
00:32:17,102 --> 00:32:19,771
YOUR WALK WAS GREAT,
BUT THE EYES WEREN'T THERE.

843
00:32:19,771 --> 00:32:22,207
Tyra: YOU ALSO HAD YOUR FIRST
PROFESSIONAL PHOTO SHOOT

844
00:32:22,207 --> 00:32:25,410
WITH THE GARDEN OF EDEN THEME,
AND HERE IS YOUR BEST SHOT.

845
00:32:26,945 --> 00:32:28,647
Xiomara: (gasps)
Nigel: WHAT DO YOU THINK?

846
00:32:28,647 --> 00:32:31,817
Xiomara: I AM SO HOT!
Janice: THIS IS AN AMPUTEE LOOK?

847
00:32:31,817 --> 00:32:33,018
THERE'S NO RIGHT ARM, YOU SEE?

848
00:32:33,018 --> 00:32:35,387
SO IF YOU FANNED AROUND
YOUR UPPER BODY,

849
00:32:35,387 --> 00:32:37,489
YOU WOULD HAVE SHOWN
A LITTLE BIT OF RIGHT ARM.

850
00:32:39,791 --> 00:32:41,460
Tyra: YOUR WALK IS OKAY,
BUT YOU DON'T KNOW WHAT TO DO

851
00:32:41,460 --> 00:32:43,528
WHEN YOU GET TO THE END
OF THE RUNWAY.

852
00:32:43,528 --> 00:32:44,463
April: OH, MY GOD!

853
00:32:45,530 --> 00:32:46,898
Janice: OKAY, FACE--FLAWLESS.

854
00:32:46,898 --> 00:32:49,835
BODY UP TO YOUR RIGHT FOOT,
YOU'RE CUTTING IT OFF

855
00:32:49,835 --> 00:32:51,336
WITH THE FAN,
UNLESS YOU WERE HIDING

856
00:32:51,336 --> 00:32:52,704
THAT YOU DIDN'T SHAVE
YOUR RIGHT LEG OR SOMETHING.

857
00:32:56,741 --> 00:32:59,044
Nigel: I NOTICE THAT
YOUR WALK IS A LITTLE STIFF.

858
00:32:59,044 --> 00:33:00,645
Catie: YEAH,
I HAD THOSE BOOTS,

859
00:33:00,645 --> 00:33:02,981
AND I'VE NEVER WALKED
IN BOOTS LIKE THAT BEFORE.

860
00:33:02,981 --> 00:33:05,050
Eric: I CAN TELL
YOU'RE SLIGHTLY UNCOMFORTABLE.

861
00:33:05,050 --> 00:33:07,219
IT LOOKS LIKE
YOUR LEG IS WOBBLING,

862
00:33:07,219 --> 00:33:08,587
AND LIKE YOU'RE ABOUT
TO FALL OVER AT ANY MINUTE.

863
00:33:10,856 --> 00:33:11,857
Tyra: SO WHAT DID YOU THINK?

864
00:33:11,857 --> 00:33:13,091
Sara: TOO BOUNCY.

865
00:33:13,091 --> 00:33:15,827
Tyra: THE BOUNCE WAS GOOD,
BUT JUST A LITTLE LESS.

866
00:33:17,229 --> 00:33:18,530
IS YOUR FINGER IN HIS MOUTH?

867
00:33:18,530 --> 00:33:20,065
Sara: OH, YEAH,
IT WAS EVERYWHERE.

868
00:33:20,065 --> 00:33:22,300
Tyra: OH, WOW!
Sara: I THINK I WAS THE ONLY EVE

869
00:33:22,300 --> 00:33:23,401
THAT TOUCHED HER ADAM.

870
00:33:25,837 --> 00:33:27,405
Nigel: THE LEG THING'S
A LITTLE UNUSUAL THERE.

871
00:33:27,405 --> 00:33:28,473
Tyra: A LITTLE MARCH.

872
00:33:28,473 --> 00:33:30,208
Yoanna: I DIDN'T THINK
I DID TOO GOOD.

873
00:33:30,208 --> 00:33:32,410
Janice: YOU HAVE
A CLASSIC FACE MADE FOR BEAUTY.

874
00:33:34,746 --> 00:33:36,114
YOU LOOK VERY SOMBER.

875
00:33:36,114 --> 00:33:38,950
NEXT TIME YOU MIGHT WANT
TO LIGHTEN IT UP.

876
00:33:38,950 --> 00:33:40,652
Camille: WOW!

877
00:33:40,652 --> 00:33:42,220
Tyra: THE ONLY THING
THAT I WOULD SAY IS

878
00:33:42,220 --> 00:33:44,289
TO KIND OF STICK YOUR BOOTY OUT
JUST A LITTLE BIT MORE

879
00:33:44,289 --> 00:33:45,957
AND GIVE IT A LITTLE "POW"!

880
00:33:48,727 --> 00:33:49,895
HI, ANNA.

881
00:33:49,895 --> 00:33:51,496
Anna: HELLO.
Tyra: HOW DO YOU FEEL ABOUT

882
00:33:51,496 --> 00:33:54,099
BEING
THE ONLY PLUS-SIZE MODEL HERE?

883
00:33:54,099 --> 00:33:56,668
Anna: I'M SURE OF MYSELF,
AND, YOU KNOW, THAT'S WHO I AM,

884
00:33:56,668 --> 00:33:58,603
SO THAT'S FINE.

885
00:33:58,603 --> 00:34:00,071
Tyra: IT LOOKED LIKE
YOU WERE MORE OF A BEAUTY QUEEN

886
00:34:00,071 --> 00:34:01,072
THAN A MODEL.

887
00:34:01,072 --> 00:34:02,240
Janice: RIGHT.
Eric: ABSOLUTELY.

888
00:34:02,240 --> 00:34:03,375
Tyra: IT LOOKED LIKE
YOU WERE LIKE, "HI, HI."

889
00:34:03,375 --> 00:34:04,743
Eric: MISS GEORGIA PEACH.

890
00:34:04,743 --> 00:34:07,345
